Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design privacy-first analytics at scale across tenants using Azure-native services with governance, data lineage, and cost discipline.

Key Concepts
- Real-time ingestion with Event Hubs and streaming processing in Databricks
- Per-tenant isolation in Delta Lake and storage governance
- Centralized model registry in Azure ML with DP-aware outputs
- Differential privacy and synthetic data for cross-tenant insights
- Purview lineage, RBAC, BYOK, DR, and cost levers

Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: apply Laplace noise for DP on a sum
function dpSum(values, epsilon) {
  const clip = values.map(v => Math.max(-1.0, Math.min(1.0, v)));
  const s = clip.reduce((a,b) => a + b, 0);
  const noise = laplace(1/epsilon);
  return s + noise;
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate Purview lineage end-to-end across all stages?
- How would you monitor privacy budget consumption and trigger data-refresh or model retraining?

## Why This Is Asked
Allocates a beginner to a practical Azure data ingestion pattern using Event Hubs, Functions, and ADLS Gen2. Emphasizes idempotency, deduplication, retries, and tenant isolation, plus basic observability and validation.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Event Hubs and capture
- Azure Functions (Event Hub trigger)
- ADLS Gen2 as sink
- Idempotent processing and de-dup with eventId
- Managed identity and security
- Backoff retries and latency validation

